  "working_tree": "Uncommitted code-intelligence work; this receipt and documentation follow frozen checks.",
  "shared_implementation": "The shared native language host uses one recording Files adapter above native I/O primitives during workspace-edit normalization. The same stateless path-set/metadata aggregate is checked by ordinary original-service validation and initial native admission in both authority profiles.",
  "contract": [
    "AnalysisContext carries a canonical bounded path set. The service HMAC binds its original native metadata aggregate together with the exact result, original request, source/overlay generations, service and issuer lifetime. Removing, replacing, reordering or adding paths cannot authorize another result. No native retained result cache is introduced.",
    "Linux/macOS metadata primitives anchor reads to a captured directory descriptor, open parents and regular data without following links, compare opened parent identity with its named entry, and capture root/parent/file identity, modification/change times, link count, mode and ownership. Access time is excluded because reads update it.",
    "Normalization records metadata before and after actual reads and directory inventories, rejects inconsistent repeated observations and rechecks the complete bounded set before publishing. Internal text aliases retain both lexical link identity/target and canonical data paths; resource-operation link rejection remains intact. Missing destinations retain the nearest missing namespace and existing parents.",
    "Flat unopened text edits and ordered resource trees use the same observer. Read-only normalization preserves existing source and workspace read limits, private runtime filtering and unchanged full resource planning policy.",
    "Ordinary ValidateAnalysis retains its checked native observation through asynchronous project/source checks and rechecks before publishing its empty original-service acknowledgement. Initial native admission checks the same original evidence under its physical lease, reproduces the shared plan/editor patch and retains the native observation through the before-execution guard.",
    "Native observations have a 16 MiB charged per-operation limit and 64 MiB shared in-flight pool, with reservations released after rejection, cancellation or drop. The public path set permits at most 16,384 records and 2 MiB of path bytes, within the unchanged 4 MiB complete response limit and 2 KiB opaque proof limit. Native traversal depth/path/read/deadline limits remain explicit. The ordinary 10,000-entry resource inventory fits the charged metadata budget.",
    "Live intelligence protocol 3 rejects older live frames. Schema 68 fences older database readers. Archived protocol-2 LanguageReview and protocol-1/2 command reviews retain their original serialized identity; accepted protocol-2 state survives upgrade/reopen and successor worker admission without the old service or grant. Fresh provider admission still requires the current live request format.",
    "Real LSP/HMAC contracts reproduce and reject restored unassociated JSON contents/modification times in ordinary validation and native lease admission for both user and paired-user profiles. Flat-file edits preserve explicit fresh review retry. Native guard checks reject metadata changes after verification without file mutation or additional LSP calls.",
    "Fresh installed resource/command/interruption and declared-input workflows pass in Local and Remote modes with the rebuilt application and native bundled host. These installed records still omit durable LanguageReview; real review-bearing initial admission is separately established by native fixtures."
  ],
